Third-party material in vfs-bench-2
===================================

vfs-bench-2 is MIT-licensed (see ../LICENSE). Each dataset's fetch.py
downloads upstream's code and data into state/, which is gitignored, at the
source pinned below, and writes into its tasks what they need of it; those
files are gitignored too.

What this directory does carry from them, each entry names: prompts and
task files quoted or adapted in a dataset's tasks, upstream sources its
graders run (datasets/<dataset>/graders/reference/), and mock servers that
reimplement upstream's services (datasets/<dataset>/mocks/). The MIT
notices that cover those follow the entries, verbatim.


Datasets
--------

AutomationBench
  Source:    https://github.com/zapier/AutomationBench
             @ 4a8e1061254004d9dac807054eed33fad7d1ff14 (v1.0.6)
  License:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Zapier, Inc., with the scope note
             below about derived API schema representations.
  Fetched:   the package, installed by uv from
             datasets/automationbench/pyproject.toml.
  Committed: its rubric's source (graders/reference/automationbench/) and
             the Monty port generated from it (graders/port.py); its API's
             schemas and endpoints (mocks/automationbench/data/); the
             mock under mocks/automationbench/ reimplements its API's
             routes and handlers; each task's instruction quotes its prompt.

