  Images:    docker.io/shivakrishnareddyma225/enterpriseops-gym-mcp-<domain>,
             by the digests datasets/enterpriseops/tools/<server>.json records
  License:   Apache-2.0 (repository and dataset). The images, which the
             repository's README tells its users to pull, carry no license
             of their own; they are taken here as part of that release.
  Fetched:   the repository and its seeds, and the dataset's tasks, by
             datasets/enterpriseops/fetch.py.
  Committed: each server's tool list as its image answers tools/list
             (tools/); the CSM image's sql/csm_schema_sqlite.sql
             (mocks/enterpriseops_csm/schema.sql); the mocks under
             mocks/enterpriseops*/ reimplement the images' tools; the tasks
             carry the dataset's prompts and verifiers; graders/index.ts
             ports benchmark/verifier.py's value extraction and comparison.

Claw-Eval
  Source:    https://github.com/claw-eval/claw-eval
             @ 5680b8b11ff2ee5dd2b07b89086a29a5c5c984d7
  License:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 claw-eval
  Fetched:   mock_services/, tasks/ and src/, by datasets/claweval/fetch.py.
  Committed: the mocks under mocks/claweval*/ reimplement its services;
             each task's instruction quotes its prompt; graders/reference/
             holds its graders' sources, verbatim, and the fields of each
             task.yaml they read; graders/port/ is built from them, and
             graders/models.ts ports its models.


ERPBench-100 (Blobfish AI's ERP Agent Simulation)
  Source:    https://github.com/blobfishai/erp-agent-simulation
             @ 5bdf458165fee71f6a7965ea30ca33dfbbce1332
  License:   code Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Blobfish AI (its LICENSE and
             NOTICE: "This product includes software developed by
             Blobfish AI."); the ERPBench-100 dataset content CC BY 4.0,
             Copyright 2026 Blobfish AI (its LICENSE-DATA).
  Fetched:   the repository, by datasets/erpbench/fetch.py.
  Committed: the tasks' instruction.md quote each task's instruction and
             list its tools' descriptions, and their workspace/tools.json
             carry the tools' descriptions and schemas;
             mocks/erpbench/world.ts ports the world's tools
             (erpbench100/world.py) to TypeScript, and graders/index.ts its
             grader (erpbench100/evaluation.py); graders/manifest.json
             carries the grader's scoring constants.


Runtime
-------

Mirage
  Source:    https://github.com/strukto-ai/mirage
             @ 9dd69a316242deddee79b40ce41aafaa2be6065c
  License:   Apache-2.0 (submodule/mirage/LICENSE)
  Included:  as a git submodule, not vendored.

Python packages for the workspace's python3
  workspace/python.py downloads these into state/python: Pyodide's builds from
  the jsDelivr CDN at the installed Pyodide's version, and pure-Python
  wheels from PyPI. Each keeps its own license, as its wheel's metadata
  states:

    et-xmlfile 2.0.0               MIT
    lxml 6.0.2                     BSD-3-Clause
    numpy 2.4.6                    BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib
                                   AND CC0-1.0
    opencv-python 4.11.0.86        Apache-2.0
    openpyxl 3.1.5                 MIT
    pandas 3.0.2                   BSD-3-Clause
    pillow 12.2.0                  MIT-CMU
    pyarrow 22.0.0                 Apache-2.0
    pymupdf 1.27.2.2               AGPL-3.0, or Artifex's commercial license
    pyodide-unix-timezones 1.0.0   MIT
    pypdf 6.21.2                   BSD-3-Clause
    python-dateutil 2.9.0.post0    Apache-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause, dual
    python-docx 1.2.0              MIT
    python-pptx 1.0.2              MIT
    pytz 2026.1.post1              MIT
    six 1.17.0                     MIT
    typing-extensions 4.15.0       PSF-2.0
    tzdata 2025.3                  Apache-2.0
    xlsxwriter 3.3.0               BSD-2-Clause

  pymupdf's AGPL applies to whoever conveys it. vfs-bench-2 only downloads
  it for local runs and never redistributes it.


